[2026-08-02T16:58:38.294Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"npm trusted publishing OIDC setup-node NODE_AUTH_TOKEN placeholder XXXXX 404 PUT registry\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"registry-url writes _authToken line that breaks npm Trusted Publisher OIDC when no NODE_AUTH_TOKEN is set · Issue #1551 · actions/setup-node\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1551\"},{\"title\":\"NPM Trusted Publishing: The “Weird” 404 Error and the Node.js 24 Fix | by Kenrick Tandrian | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@kenricktan11/npm-trusted-publishers-the-weird-404-error-and-the-node-js-24-fix-a9f1d717a5dd\"},{\"title\":\"How to set up trusted publishing for npm | remarkablemark\",\"url\":\"https://remarkablemark.org/blog/2025/12/19/npm-trusted-publishing/\"},{\"title\":\"NPM publish using OIDC on github actions · community · Discussion #176761\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/176761\"},{\"title\":\"Trusted publishing for npm packages | npm Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers/\"},{\"title\":\"npm-trusted-publishing | Skills Mark...\",\"url\":\"https://lobehub.com/skills/pr-pm-prpm-npm-trusted-publishing\"},{\"title\":\"npm Trusted Publishing and GitHub Actions - Nick Radford\",\"url\":\"https://nickradford.dev/blog/npm-trusted-publishing-and-github-actions\"},{\"title\":\"Seamless OIDC Publishing to npmjs with Yarn & GitHub Actions | devActivity\",\"url\":\"https://devactivity.com/posts/development-integrations/solving-the-not-found-error-seamless-oidc-publishing-to-npmjs-with-yarn-in-github-actions/\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/RequestNetwork/web-components/pull/345\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about npm trusted publishing with OIDC and the 404 PUT registry error you're inquiring about.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**The 404 PUT Error Issue:**\nWhen the OIDC handshake fails, the registry treats you as an anonymous user, and anonymous users can't PUT (publish), resulting in the misleading 404 Not Found.\n\n**Common Causes:**\n\n1. **npm CLI Version:** Trusted Publishing now requires npm CLI version 11.5.1 or later. Node.js 22 ships with npm v10, while Node.js 24 (LTS) ships with npm v11. Because Node 22 uses npm v10, the CLI doesn't support the latest OIDC handshake protocols required by the registry.\n\n2. **setup-node Configuration:** When registry-url is set, actions/setup-node always writes // /:_authToken=${N…KEN} to .npmrc, which is correct for the classic token-auth flow, but silently breaks the npm Trusted Publisher (OIDC) flow when no NODE_AUTH_TOKEN is set.\n\n**Solutions:**\n\n- Update npm to version 11.5.1 or later before publishing\n- For Trusted Publisher OIDC, set auth-token-line: [REDACTED] in setup-node to write only the registry= line\n- Do not set NODE_AUTH_TOKEN when using OIDC trusted publishing\n\nThe search results indicate these are well-documented issues in the GitHub Actions and npm communities with established workarounds.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
