[2026-08-02T16:58:51.791Z] [INFO]         "content": "# Summary of GitHub Issue #1551\n\n## What Breaks\nWhen `registry-url` is set in `actions/setup-node`, the action writes an `_authToken` line to `.npmrc` even when no `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN` is configured. This silently breaks npm's Trusted Publisher (OIDC) authentication flow because npm sees the empty auth token, assumes authentication is already configured, and never initiates the OIDC token exchange. The publish then fails with `ENEEDAUTH` or `E404`.\n\n## Reproduction\nUsing the recommended Trusted Publisher setup with `id-token: [REDACTED] permissions and no `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN` secret configured, `npm publish --provenance` fails despite having valid OIDC credentials available.\n\n## Current Workaround\nStrip the problematic line after setup-node runs:\n```bash\nnpmrc=\"${NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG:-$HOME/.npmrc}\"\nsed -i '/\\_authToken/d' \"$npmrc\"\n```\nAfter removal, npm detects the OIDC environment variables and successfully completes authentication.\n\n## Status of `auth-token-line`\n**Not implemented.** The issue proposes three solutions, with option (1)—a new `auth-token-line: [REDACTED] input—being the most back-compatible. The issue was opened May 17, 2026, and remains open without an implemented fix or confirmed release in current setup-node versions."
[2026-08-02T16:58:51.791Z] [INFO]       }
