[2026-08-02T17:04:06.413Z] [INFO]         "type": "text",
[2026-08-02T17:04:06.413Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   The user asked me to solve GitHub issue https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-language/issues/191 (\"Check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD and fix them all\") on the prepared branch `issue-191-66112f3ba3f7` in `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1785689586800`, updating the existing PR https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-language/pull/192.\n\n   Verbatim user instructions:\n   - \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/191/pulls/192 folder.\"\n   - \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n   - \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n   - \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n   - \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n   - \"Proceed.\"\n\n   The issue body itself requires: comparing all CI/CD files against three templates (`link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`, `js-...`, `python-...`), reporting the same issue in the templates if found there, following `https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`, and planning + executing everything in a single pull request until every requirement is fully addressed.\n\n   Standing constraints from session guidance: do not call the Agent tool or Workflow/deep-research (not requested by the user); never log environment variables or token values; push only to branch `issue-191-66112f3ba3f7`; update PR 192 with `gh pr edit`; run local CI checks before pushing; `gh pr ready 192` when finished.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GitHub Actions workflows (`.github/workflows/js.yml`, `.github/workflows/rust.yml`)\n   - npm OIDC trusted publishing (requires npm CLI >= 11.5.1, Node >= 22.14.0, `permissions: id-token: [REDACTED], trusted publisher configured on npmjs.com matching repo + workflow filename)\n   - `actions/setup-node@v6` `registry-url` writing `//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${N…KEN}` and exporting placeholder `XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX` (actions/setup-node issue #1551)\n   - Sigstore provenance (`npm publish --provenance`) is independent of registry auth\n   - `NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG` npmrc sanitization; deprecated `always-auth` key\n   - Concurrency control: repository-scoped writer group `release-${{ github.repository }}-main-write` with `cancel-in-progress: false`; cancellable read-only `check-*` groups\n   - `!cancelled()` vs `always()` in job conditions\n   - Rust CI: clippy pedantic, rustfmt, `RUSTFLAGS: -Dwarnings`, `cargo llvm-cov --fail-under-lines 84.30`, changelog.d fragments, crate size checks\n   - JS/Rust parity manifest gate (`parity/language-features.json`, `js/scripts/check-js-rust-parity.mjs`)\n   - secretlint repository scan\n   - Cross-workflow release dispatch (`gh workflow run js.yml --ref main -f release_version=...`)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`.github/workflows/js.yml`** (MODIFIED) — The failing workflow. Two jobs: `test` (JavaScript Package) and `publish` (Publish npm Package). The publish job is the source of the current CI failure.\n     Edit 1 — inserted a new step after \"Update npm for trusted publishing\":\n     ```yaml\n      # actions/setup-node writes `_authToken=${N…KEN}` and exports the\n      # placeholder `XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX` whenever no token is supplied. npm\n      # then skips the OIDC exchange and the registry rejects the anonymous PUT\n      # with a misleading `E404`. Strip that placeholder so trusted publishing is\n      # actually attempted; keep it when a real NPM_TOKEN bootstrap secret exists.\n      # See actions/setup-node#1551 and issue #191.\n      - name: Prepare npm authentication\n        id: npm_auth\n        env:\n          NPM_TOKEN: [REDACTED] secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n          PACKAGE_NAME: meta-language\n          PUBLISH_WORKFLOW_FILE: .github/workflows/js.yml\n          # Set to '1' (or add --verbose) to trace npm credential resolution.\n          NPM_AUTH_DEBUG: ${{ vars.NPM_AUTH_DEBUG }}\n        run: node scripts/prepare-npm-auth.mjs\n        working-directory: js\n     ```\n     Edit 2 — replaced the \"Publish to npm\" step and added a failure explainer:\n     ```yaml\n      - name: Publish to npm\n        if: steps.npm.outputs.already_published != 'true'\n        # Optional NPM_TOKEN bootstrap fallback. OIDC trusted publishing is the\n        # steady-state mechanism; the token path only matters until a trusted\n        # publisher is configured for the package on npmjs.com.\n        env:\n          NODE_AUTH_TOKEN: [REDACTED] secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n        run: npm publish --provenance\n        working-directory: js\n\n      - name: Explain npm publish failure\n        if: failure() && steps.npm.outputs.already_published != 'true'\n        env:\n          AUTH_MODE: ${{ steps.npm_auth.outputs.auth_mode }}\n        run: |\n          echo \"::error::npm publish failed with auth mode '$AUTH_MODE'.\"\n          if [ \"$AUTH_MODE\" = \"oidc\" ]; then\n            echo \"An E404 on PUT https://registry.npmjs.org/meta-language means the registry\"\n            echo \"treated the request as anonymous. Confirm that meta-language has a trusted\"\n            echo \"publisher on npmjs.com pointing at ${{ github.repository }} and workflow file\"\n            echo \".github/workflows/js.yml, or set an NPM_TOKEN secret to bootstrap the publish.\"\n          fi\n     ```\n\n   - **`js/scripts/prepare-npm-auth.mjs`** (CREATED) — The core fix. Pure, testable functions plus a CLI. Verbose diagnostics default OFF (per user requirement). Never logs token values, only npmrc key names.\n     Key exports/signatures:\n     ```js\n     export const SETUP_NODE_PLACEHOLDER_TOKEN = 'XXX…XXX';\n     const AUT…INE = /^[^\\S\\r\\n]*(?:\\/\\/[^\\s=]*:)?_authToken[^\\S\\r\\n]*=.*(?:\\r?\\n|$)/gim;\n     const ALWAYS_AUTH_LINE = /^[^\\S\\r\\n]*always-auth[^\\S\\r\\n]*=.*(?:\\r?\\n|$)/gim;\n\n     export function isUsableToken(token)            // false for '', placeholder, '${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}'\n     export function resolveAuthMode(env)            // 'token' | 'oidc' | 'none'\n     export function sanitizeNpmrc(content, { keepAuthToken = [REDACTED] })\n       // -> { content, removedAuthToken, removedAlwaysAuth }\n     export function buildMissingCredentialGuidance(packageName, repository, workflow)\n     export function prepareNpmAuth({ env, logger, verbose, fileExists, readFile, writeFile })\n       // -> { mode, path, changed, skipped }\n     ```\n     `resolveAuthMode` returns `'token'` if `NPM_TOKEN` or `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN` is usable, `'oidc'` if both `ACT…URL` and `ACT…KEN` are set, otherwise `'none'`.\n     CLI main block:\n     ```js\n     const verbose = process.argv.includes('--verbose') || process.env.NPM_AUTH_DEBUG === '1';\n     const { mode } = prepareNpmAuth({ verbose });\n     if (process.env.GITHUB_OUTPUT) {\n       writeFileSync(process.env.GITHUB_OUTPUT, `auth_mode=${mode}\\n`, { flag: 'a' });\n     }\n     if (mode === 'none') { /* ::error:: + guidance, process.exit(1) */ }\n     ```\n\n   - **`js/tests/package-release.test.js`** (READ, MUST BE UPDATED — will now fail) — Contains assertions that lock in the broken state:\n     ```js\n     assert.doesNotMatch(workflow, /NODE_AUTH_TOKEN/);\n     ...\n     assert.doesNotMatch(rustWorkflow, /npm publish|npm view|NODE_AUTH_TOKEN/);\n     ```\n     Also asserts `registry-url`, `npm publish --provenance`, `id-token: [REDACTED], writer concurrency group, `REQUESTED_VERSION` env indirection, and that both rust `auto-release`/`manual-release` jobs have `actions: write` and `gh workflow run js.yml --ref main` after \"Create GitHub Release\".\n\n   - **`.github/workflows/rust.yml`** (READ, 1050+ lines) — Jobs: detect-changes, changelog, version-check, secrets-scan, fresh-merge, cargo-lock, lint, test (matrix), coverage, build, auto-release, manual-release, changelog-pr, deploy-docs. No longer publishes npm; dispatches js.yml at line ~734. Coverage job has the good `if: env.CODECOV_TOKEN != ''` + `::notice::` skip pattern to emulate.\n\n   - **`js/package.json`** — name `meta-language`, version `0.58.0`, scripts: `test` (`node --test tests/*.test.js`), `check:parity`, `check:parity:manifest`.\n\n   - **`dev/log/issues/191/pulls/192/ci-logs/`** (CREATED) — `run-30735100706.log`, `run-30733403030.log`, `run-30708127649.log`, `run-30240588949.log`, `run-30166422548.log`, `run-30734654534-js-success.log`, `run-30734654535-js-success.log`, `run-30732901520-rust-success.log`.\n   - **`dev/log/issues/191/pulls/192/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`** (CREATED, 401 lines) — fetched from link-assistant/hive-mind.\n   - **`dev/log/issues/191/pulls/192/templates/{js,rust,python}/`** (CREATED) — shallow clones of the three template repos.\n\n   - **Template reference `templates/js/.github/workflows/release.yml`** — the NPM_TOKEN bootstrap fallback pattern (lines ~497-505, ~575-578) with the comment referencing template issue #77; `templates/js/scripts/sanitize-npm-userconfig.mjs` (removes only `always-auth`, NOT `_authToken` — so the templates share the same latent bug).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Primary CI error — `npm error code E404 Not Found - PUT https://registry.npmjs.org/meta-language`** (runs 30735100706, 30733403030). Root cause found and verified: `actions/setup-node@v6` with `registry-url` writes `_authToken=${N…KEN}` into `$NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG` and exports the placeholder `XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX`; npm 11.19.0 therefore believes it is authenticated, skips the OIDC handshake, and the registry rejects the anonymous PUT as 404. Confirmed by actions/setup-node#1551. Fix in progress: new `prepare-npm-auth.mjs` strips the placeholder line so OIDC is genuinely attempted, plus an `NPM_TOKEN` bootstrap fallback and an actionable failure explainer.\n   - **Historical CI error — `npm error code ENEEDAUTH`** in the Rust workflow's Auto Release job (runs 30240588949, 30166422548) for meta-language@0.55.0 with empty `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN`. Same root cause family; that npm publish path was already removed from rust.yml in favour of dispatching js.yml.\n   - **Historical CI error — parity gate** (run 30708127649): `parity: javascript-parser-codegen rust evidence does not exist: rust/changelog.d/20260619_233000_javascript_parser_codegen.md`. Already fixed on main; local `npm run check:parity` now passes.\n   - **Self-inflicted issue not yet fixed:** my js.yml edits add `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN`, which breaks the existing assertion `assert.doesNotMatch(workflow, /NODE_AUTH_TOKEN/)` in `js/tests/package-release.test.js`. That test must be updated to assert the new intended state.\n   - **Minor tool mistakes I corrected:** ran `grep` in a stale working directory (`No such file or directory`) and mis-mapped run IDs to workflows (30734654535 was Rust, not JS) — both corrected by re-running with absolute paths and re-downloading the right logs.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Solved: identified with direct log evidence + upstream confirmation the exact reason npm releases have been failing since at least v0.55.0 — the setup-node placeholder `_authToken` silently disables OIDC trusted publishing. Also established the repo has NO `NPM_TOKEN` secret at repo or org level (org has only `CARGO_TOKEN`, `DOCKERHUB_TOKEN`, `NUGET_API_KEY`), and that the `meta-language` package exists on npm at 0.46.0 (maintainer konard), so a trusted publisher CAN be configured. Discovered the regression history: issue #177 removed `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN` expecting OIDC to take over, and a test now enforces that broken state.\n   Ongoing: writing tests for the new script; updating `package-release.test.js`; writing the deep-analysis/timeline/requirements/root-cause documents into `dev/log/issues/191/pulls/192/`; auditing remaining template-vs-repo gaps; filing upstream issues.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The single user message was the task prompt: \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-language/issues/191 / Your prepared branch: issue-191-66112f3ba3f7 / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1785689586800 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-language/pull/192 / Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/191/pulls/192 folder. / Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help. / If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off. / If the issue is related to another reposi