[2026-08-02T17:23:33.087Z] [INFO]           "command": "gh issue comment 1440 --repo actions/setup-node --body \"Data point for anyone landing here from a still-failing \\`E404\\`: the fix in #1558 shipped only on the v7 line. \\`@v6\\` (currently v6.5.0) still exports the placeholder — \\`dist/setup/index.js\\` on \\`v6\\` contains \\`XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX\\`, on \\`v7\\` it does not, and the v6.5.0 tag and the #1558 merge commit are on diverged branches. So projects pinned to \\`@v6\\` remain affected even though the issue is closed.\n\nConcretely, with \\`actions/setup-node@v6\\` (SHA \\`249970729cb0ef3589644e2896645e5dc5ba9c38\\\"), node 24.18.0 and npm 11.19.0, and no token set anywhere in the workflow, every step of the job still shows \\`NODE_AUTH_TOKEN: XXX…\\` and \\`npm publish --provenance\\` fails with \\`404 Not Found - PUT https://registry.npmjs.org/<package>\\`.\n\nTwo workarounds, for whichever is easier: move to \\`@v7\\`, or strip the line before publishing, which is version-agnostic:\n\n\\`\\`\\`bash\nsed -i '/_authToken/d' \\\"\\$NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG\\\"\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nWould a backport of #1558 to the v6 branch be considered?\" 2>&1 | tail -2",
