[2026-08-02T17:24:04.625Z] [INFO]   "result": "Done. PR #192 is ready for review: https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-language/pull/192\n\n**Root cause.** npm releases have been broken since 0.55.0 (last published version on npm is 0.46.0). `actions/setup-node` with `registry-url` unconditionally writes `//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${N…KEN}` into `$NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG` and exports the placeholder `XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX`. npm then believes it is authenticated, **skips the OIDC exchange**, and the registry rejects the anonymous upload as `404` — hence the misleading `E404`. The placeholder is visible in every step of our own failing job even though the workflow set no token. With an empty token the same line produced the earlier `ENEEDAUTH`.\n\nI verified the upstream state rather than taking the closed issue at face value: `actions/setup-node#1551` was closed as a duplicate with a maintainer saying OIDC worked for them, but `#1440` was ultimately resolved by merging PR #1558, which removes the dummy token — and that fix shipped **only on v7**. I diffed the built bundles: `v6`'s `dist/setup/index.js` still contains the placeholder, `v7`'s does not, and the tags are on diverged branches.\n\n**Fix.** `js/scripts/prepare-npm-auth.mjs` resolves the auth mode, strips the placeholder line so OIDC actually runs, removes the deprecated `always-auth` key, and exits non-zero with remediation instructions when no credential exists — instead of surfacing a bare `E404`. Verbose tracing is off by default (`NPM_AUTH_DEBUG=1`) and never prints values, which is covered by a test.\n\nNotable false negative: `js/tests/package-release.test.js` asserted `doesNotMatch(workflow, /NODE_AUTH_TOKEN/)`, so the suite was actively defending the unpublishable configuration. Replaced with assertions for the intended state.\n\n**Upstream reports filed:** the JS template carries the same latent bug (its sanitizer strips only `always-auth`) — link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template#120, with reproduction, workaround, and code fix. Also commented the v6-backport gap on actions/setup-node#1440. The Rust and Python templates are unaffected; neither publishes to npm.\n\n**Verification:** JavaScript workflow — success; Rust workflow — success (all jobs green; Coverage/release jobs skipped as designed). Locally 89 tests pass, parity clean, secretlint clean over the ~70k lines of run logs committed under `dev/log/issues/191/pulls/192/` alongside `ANALYSIS.md` and `UPSTREAM-REPORTS.md`. Working tree is clean.\n\nOne thing I could not do from a PR: publishing also requires a trusted publisher registered for `meta-language` on npmjs.com pointing at this repo and `.github/workflows/js.yml`. That is account-side configuration. Until it exists, an `NPM_TOKEN` secret takes over via the bootstrap path — and either way the job now states which one is missing.",
